}}
{{Leashnotes
| name = Pounce
| desc = Stops {{M|forced movement}} when the {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|slark_pounce_[[leash]]}} expires while the forced movement is happening.
}}
{{Draftnotes
| name = Slark Pounce
| desc = Requires drafting {{A|Slark|Essence Shift}} for its corresponding facet component to work.
}}

 {{Leashcard}}

* {{hi|Slark}} {{Symbol|Facing Angle|r}} [[File:Dota2 Slark Pounce Visualized icon-1-1.png|84px]][[File:Dota2 Slark Pounce Visualized icon-1-2.png|84px]]
** Can affect an enemy hero at max {{#expr:{{#var:Pounce value1}}+{{#var:Pounce value2}}/2}} ({{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{ValueColor||{{#expr:{{#var:Pounce value1 agh}}+{{#var:Pounce value2}}/2}}|agh}})-distance away from Slark's current cast position, point [[File:Dota2 Letter-o.png|21px|O]] and latch radius [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|21px|P]] .
** {{Symbol|Leash}}
*** [[Wikipedia:Circle|Circle]] [[File:Dota2 Letter-f.png|21px|F]] is the [[leash]] radius. The affected enemy hero can only move a limited distance, with reduced set {{M|movement speed}} values, away from point [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|21px|P]] , Slark's landing position.
*** {{Symbol|Projectile|Link}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
**** Unlike other Leash sources, this source does not break by default if the victim is outside the maximum distance due to {{M|forced movement}}.
**** The following sources break the leash:
***** {{A|Harpoon|Draw Forth}}
***** {{A|Hurricane Pike|Hurricane Thrust}}
***** If the victim goes beyond the leash range by forced movement and issues a move command.
* The ability effects are applied as follows:
** {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
**# Applies {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|slark_pounce_[[leash]]}} if the unit within the latch radius is an enemy hero.
**#* {{Symbol|Leash}} {{to}} [[File:Dota2 Slark Pounce Radius icon-2.png|84px]]
**#** Checks the affected enemy hero's current position and {{M|facing angle}} per {{M|server tick}} to centerpoint [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|21px|P]] within Circle [[File:Dota2 Letter-f.png|21px|F]] , then applies the [[Movement Speed#Set Movement Speed|set]] {{M|movement speed}} value accordingly when it is facing away from the centerpoint.
**#*** The further the affected unit to the centerpoint the potent the effect.
**#*** The set movement speed value is '''not''' reflected on the [[HUD]].
**#** Considers {{M|clones}} as heroes, {{M|illusions}}, and {{M|creep-heroes}} as creeps.
**#** Affects the following units:
**#*** {{M|Invisible}} units.
**#** Does not affect the following units:
**#*** {{M|Hidden}} units.
**#*** {{M|Invulnerable}} units.
**# Applies {{A|Slark|Essence Shift}} debuff stacks corresponding of its level.
** {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
**# Grants Slark the following ability effects upon cast:
**#* Does not {{M|disjoint}} incoming {{M|projectiles}} upon cast.
**#* {{Symbol|Modifier|Buff}} {{Code|slark_pounce}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Caster|Leap}}
**#** {{M|Disarm}}
**#** The buff duration has a fixed duration, and functions as the ability cast downtime. Slark cannot recast the ability while the buff is active.
**#** Applies a non-disabling {{M|upward movement}}, and leaps at {{#expr:{{#var:Pounce basic3}}}} ({{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{ValueColor||{{#expr:{{#var:Pounce value1 agh}}/({{#var:Pounce basic1}}) round2}}|agh}})-speed over {{#var:Pounce basic1}} seconds, toward Slark's current {{M|facing angle}}.
**#*** {{cf|aghnotes}} Hence, increasing the leap distance increases the leap speed.
**#*** {{cf|expr}}
**#**** {{Code|BaseLeapSpeed {{=}} LeapDistance / {{#var:Pounce basic1}}}}
**#**** {{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{Code|LeapSpeed [[Aghanim's Scepter|Agh]] {{=}} AghLeapDistance / BaseLeapSpeed}}
**#* {{Symbol|Turn Rate}} {{Symbol|fx|v}}
**#** Does not lock Slark's facing angle.
**#** The leap duration varies depending on the terrain.
**#** Can leap over other units and {{M|impassable terrain}}.
**# Slark is issued an attack order on the affected enemy upon the {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|slark_pounce_leash}} debuff application, regardless of auto-attack settings.
**#* Applies {{A|Slark|Essence Shift}} of its corresponding level.
**# {{Symbol|Trees}}
**#* [[Trees]] within 100-radius are destroyed upon landing.

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Pounce icon0}}
| desc = Slark leaps forward, leashing and applying Essence Shift stacks to the first hero he connects. That unit can only move a limited distance away from Slark's landing position.
}}
* {{Symbol|Leash}} {{to}} [[File:Dota2 Slark Pounce Radius icon-1.png|84px]]
** {{Symbol|Modifier|Debuff}} {{Code|slark_pounce_leash}} checks if the affected enemy hero ({{Code|H}}) is facing or facing away from centerpoint [[File:Dota2 Letter-p.png|21px|P]] .
** The [[Movement Speed#Set Movement Speed|set]] {{M|movement speed}} has the following properties:
*** The affected enemy hero has a base 140-set movement speed at 360-distance from the centerpoint.
*** Applies a {{Code|4}} set movement speed reduction per 1-distance away from the [[leash]]ed point ({{Code|P}}), up to a max 0.1-set movement speed value.
** {{cf|expr}}
*** Circle [[File:Dota2 Letter-f.png|21px|F]] and [[File:Dota2 Letter-b.png|21px|B]] have {{#var:Pounce type1 value1}}-radius and 360-radius respectively in the diagram.
*** The set movement speed formulas are defined as follows:
**** {{Code|360 < ( E - P ) < 394.975}} {{to}} {{Code|SetMS {{=}} 1580 - 4 × (E - P)}}
**** {{Code|394.975 < ( E - P ) < {{#var:Pounce type1 value1}}}} {{to}} {{Code|SetMS {{=}} 0.1}}
**** {{Code|360 ≤ ( E - P ) {{=}} {{#var:Pounce type1 value1}}}} {{to}} {{Code|SetMS {{=}} Inactive}}
<hr>
* {{cf|aghnotes}} Acquiring the {{M|Aghanim's Scepter|text=ability upgrade}} immediately grants {{ValueColor||1|agh}} extra charge.

* The Following Sources can't move unit at all:
** {{A|Clockwerk|Jetpack}}
** {{A|Earth Spirit|Geomagnetic Grip}}
** {{I|Force Boots}}
** {{I|Force Staff}}
** {{A|Marci|Rebound (Alt-Cast)}}
* The Following Sources can't move unit outside the Leash Range:
** {{A|Huskar|Inner Fire}}
** {{A|Magnus|Skewer}}
** {{A|Magnus|Shockwave}}
** {{A|Phoenix|Toggle Movement}}
** {{A|Snapfire|Firesnap Cookie}}
** {{M|Fear}} sources
** {{M|Taunt}} sources

* The Following Ally Sources can move unit outside the Leash Range:
** {{A|Earth Spirit|Boulder Smash}}
** {{A|Largo|Catchy Lick}}
** {{A|Pudge|Meat Hook}}
** {{A|Tiny|Toss}}
** {{A|Wind Waker|Cyclone}}

* The Following Ally Sources break the Leash:
** {{A|Harpoon|Draw Forth}}
** {{A|Hurricane Pike|Hurricane Thrust}}

* The Following Objects can move unit outside the Leash Range:
** {{A|Clockwerk|Power Cogs}}
** {{A|Drow Ranger|Glacier}}
